      ["Do not separate duty from acceptance", "Service conditions such as the vehicle's braking arrangement and operating environment provide context for the approved requirement. They do not let a purchasing team invent its own friction or thermal acceptance values. Obtain the qualification and production evidence required for the actual specification. A laboratory result belongs to its tested material, configuration and method; it cannot be extended to every part using the same marketing label."],
      ["Keep replacement approval and receiving inspection distinct", "Receiving checks verify the identity, condition and required evidence of the delivered item. They do not authorize a new material pairing. If the proposed brake shoe differs from the approved specification, resolve that difference through engineering before placing a production order. Preserve the accepted material and drawing references on the purchase order, packing list and supplier release documentation."]
